  "comment": "What the app installs the engine's Python environment from. Pins are exact. uv is downloaded from its GitHub release and checked against the SHA-256 below before it is run; uv itself checks the Python build it downloads (the pinned uv version carries that checksum table). Packages come from the engine bundle (bundle.json, requirements.lock with hashes). Change a pin here and in docs/desktop-profile.md together. The llamacpp pins are the release archives of ggml-org/llama.cpp (sizes and SHA-256 as GitHub publishes them, re-checked by downloading); only the Apple-silicon build uses a GPU, the others are processor builds until a CUDA or Vulkan variant is chosen (docs/phase2-stage-d-plan.md).",
